From 56105d19be28fff3ff9740445b88ad3308162f39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Killy <308386066+killy-netsphere@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:43:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 006/211] cuda: twin device objects for twin backends

ggml_backend_sched decides copy-or-in-place by the buffer type device object, so a second backend on the same ggml device
read the primary activations in place with no event ordering. A twin backend now has its own device object (same CUDA
device, name CUDAn_twin) and buffer type; cross-backend tensors are copied with the CUDA backend event ordering. The MoE
cache identifies the physical device by the PCI bus id.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
